AmiScreamer - the programs
==========================

AmiScreamer is a port of the OpenScreamer engine to the Amiga (68040, 68060, 68080) and to MorphOS.
OpenScreamer by Danik: https://github.com/ItsDanik/openscreamer

This drawer holds only the programs, for updating an existing installation: copy the programs into the game's drawer
(where DATA/, GFX/, CONFIG/ and MUSIC/ are). A new installation with game data, title logo and music is done by the
installation package (AmiScreamer_Install, "Install!").

  amiscreamer_080                  game for Vampire (68080)
  amiscreamer_060                  game for 68060
  amiscreamer_040                  game for 68040
  amiscreamer_mos                  game for MorphOS (PowerPC)
  amiscreamer_launcher             the launcher (MUI), with Catalogs/ for German
  amiscreamer_server               network server for AmigaOS (optional)
  amiscreamer_server_mos           network server for MorphOS (optional)
  Linux/amiscreamer_server_x64     network server for Linux, PC (optional)
  Linux/amiscreamer_server_arm64   network server for Linux, arm64, e.g. Raspberry Pi 3/4/5 (optional)

The launcher starts the game; its settings (CONFIG/AMIGA.CFG: screen, sound, AHI mode, network, pad buttons) stay
valid. The launcher here has no title logo, only the installation adds it: if you already have an installed
launcher ("Screamer" or "Bleifuss"), simply keep it.

The game keeps its own files (amiscreamer.cfg, records, championship, replays) in its drawer.


